<newsitem itemid="434590" id="root" date="1997-03-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Independent Insurance yearly profits rise.</title>
<headline>Independent Insurance yearly profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			    (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p>	    Shr (pence)	     57.5 vs 48.3</p>
<p>	    Dividend (pence)	 13.25 11.25</p>
<p>	    Pretax profit		52.0 35.5</p>
<p>	    Gross written premiums 438.9 410.5</p>
<p>NOTE - The pretax figure includes realised investment gains. Excluding realised investment gains, pretax profit rose to 40.2 million stg from 33.3 million. The total pretax figure also includes a first provision of 2.1 million stg for equalisation reserves, designed to smooth the impact of adverse underwriting results and which became a legal requirement in 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
